This directory contains the main SQLite copy used by Mozilla storage
(mozStorage).

Current version: SQLite 3.53.4
Source: sqlite-amalgamation-3530400.zip from https://www.sqlite.org/
SQLite source id:
2026-07-24 19:02:57 bf7c7f30031888f4e796e429ab3978879485813aaca6f641c7b33e4e09459bcc

The previous ZoolRunner/RetroZilla copy identified as SQLite 3.3.5 in
sqlite3.h, although this file previously claimed 3.3.4.  It was compared
against SQLite's Fossil tag version-3.3.5:

  manifest.uuid a091a61d8832ad3454231f480ec605101bb9363a

Local changes found in the old copy:

* src/Makefile.in integrated SQLite into the Mozilla configure/make build.
* sqlite3-param-indexes.patch added sqlite3_bind_parameter_indexes() and
  sqlite3_free_parameter_indexes() for mozStorage's repeated named-parameter
  binding behavior.
* preload-cache.patch added sqlite3Preload() and private pager changes for
  mozIStorageConnection.preload().
* mozStorageAsyncIO.cpp and sqlite3file.h used SQLite 3.3-era private OsFile
  hooks exposed through SQLITE_ENABLE_REDEF_IO.
* sqlite-fix-non-unicode-win.patch changed the old Windows OS layer to handle
  non-Unicode Windows paths.
* os_os2.c, os_os2.h, os_beos.c, and os.h changes retained OS/2 and BeOS OS
  layer support in the split 3.3.x source.
* Several files contained upstream post-3.3.5 fixes from SQLite CVS, including
  parser, pager, UTF, optimizer, shell, Tcl, and allocation fixes.

The 3.53.4 update uses the upstream amalgamation directly and keeps local
integration in src/Makefile.in, src/config.h, src/sqlite.def, and
src/sqlite3compat.c.

The mozStorage duplicate-parameter APIs are preserved in sqlite3compat.c using
modern public sqlite3_bind_parameter_* APIs.

sqlite3Preload() is preserved as a public entry point for the historical
mozIStorageConnection.preload() API.  Modern SQLite no longer exposes the
private pager entry points used by the old implementation, so ZoolRunner now
implements preload as a public-API best-effort scan using PRAGMA quick_check
for each attached database.

The old SQLite async-I/O hook has not been ported.  It depended on private
SQLite 3.3 OsFile structures and sqlite3_os_switch(), both replaced upstream by
SQLite's VFS architecture.  mozStorage's service methods remain present and are
synchronous no-ops so application-facing XPCOM storage APIs are unchanged.

The old split-source OS/2 and BeOS SQLite OS layers were not textually carried
forward into the 3.53.4 amalgamation.  Restoring those targets, if still
required with MOZ_STORAGE enabled, should be handled as VFS portability work
against modern SQLite rather than by reapplying the obsolete SQLite 3.3 OsFile
implementation.

Important compile-time options:

* SQLITE_THREADSAFE=1
* SQLITE_SECURE_DELETE=1
* SQLITE_OMIT_LOAD_EXTENSION=1
* SQLITE_CUSTOM_INCLUDE=config.h

For VC6-era Windows builds, config.h disables MSVC intrinsics and SEH and
selects conservative non-NT Win32 behavior:

* SQLITE_DISABLE_INTRINSIC=1
* SQLITE_OMIT_SEH=1
* SQLITE_WIN32_NO_WIDE=1
* SQLITE_OS_WINNT=0
* SQLITE_OMIT_WAL=1
* SQLITE_MAX_MMAP_SIZE=0

Those settings are intended to keep the source conservative for legacy Windows
builds.  They still require validation in an actual VC6/NT 3.51/Windows 95
environment.
